{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A Song of Ascents. To You I have lifted up</b> — the poet speaks concerning the great one of the generation, who is in exile or under siege; therefore, \"to You I have lifted up.\"" "And the meaning of <b>who sit in the heavens</b> — because all the decrees come from there."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 123, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:12.248711291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}